      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-45490 is a .NET SDK elevation of privilege issue: the dotnet workload command uses a named pipe with a weak access control list, so one local user can create or truncate files as another local user. Microsoft states that it only affects .NET on Windows operating systems, and lists .NET 10.0 SDK 10.0.100 through 10.0.108 as affected and 10.0.109 as fixed (https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/403, https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-45490, https://github.com/dotnet/core/blob/main/release-notes/10.0/10.0.9/10.0.9.md). DHI dotnet10-runtime for Alpine 3.24 builds .NET 10 for Linux, and the .NET SDK it ships in dotnet10-runtime-bootstrap is built for Linux (linux-musl), where the Windows-only named-pipe code path is not used, so the vulnerable code is not reached. For reference, the bootstrap SDK is 10.0.108 in 10.0.8-r0 and 10.0.109 or later from 10.0.9-r0 on."
